        "original_id": "33789ba0-d550-51ff-b5ce-92d3f6461bd2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Breach\n- People: Billy Ray, Adam Mazer, William Rotko, Robert Hanssen, Eric O'Neill, Ryan Phillippe, Francis M. Mullen Jr.\n- Organizations: Federal Bureau of Investigation, Drug Enforcement Administration, Soviet intelligence, Russian intelligence\n- Topics: film production, espionage, FBI careers\n\nFacts:\n- Francis M. \"Bud\" Mullen Jr. was born on December 14, 1934, in New London, Connecticut.\n- Robert Philip Hanssen was born on April 18, 1944.\n- Robert Hanssen was a Federal Bureau of Investigation agent who spied for Soviet and Russian intelligence services against the United States from 1979 to 2001.\n- Robert Hanssen was convicted of spying for the Soviet Union and later Russia for more than two decades.\n- Francis M. Mullen Jr. served as Executive Assistant Director of the Federal Bureau of Investigation and as Administrator of the Drug Enforcement Administration.\n- In the 2000s, Ryan Phillippe appeared in the films Gosford Park (2001), Crash (2004), Flags of Our Fathers (2006), Breach (2007), and Stop-Loss (2008).\n- Breach is a 2007 American historical and political thriller film directed by Billy Ray.\n- The screenplay for Breach was written by Billy Ray, Adam Mazer, and William Rotko.\n- Breach is based on the true story of Robert Hanssen and Eric O'Neill, who worked as Hanssen's assistant and helped bring about Hanssen's downfall.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
